# Alembic Migrations

Generic single-database configuration.

## Creating New Migrations

As a best practice, please use a timestamp for the revision id and include a
short descriptive message when creating new migrations:

For example:

```sh
alembic revision --autogenerate --rev-id $(date +%Y%m%d%H%M) -m "Added new table."
```

## Applying and Removing New Migrations

Migrations are automatically applied through the Sensemaking container to the database, but during development it can be beneficial to apply and revert while fleshing out schema changes:

```sh
# apply new migration
alembic upgrade head

# revert migration
alembic downgrade -1

# view history
alembic history
```
